<body>
    <h1>Use Case 2.1.6.3.2: Admin Creates Custom Landing Page for Creates C=
ampaign Setup (Step-3.2)</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><strong>User Story</strong></p>
<p>As an Admin, I want to create a custom landing page by either importing =
an existing site or adding my custom content directly, so that I can simula=
te a personalized phishing experience for users.</p>
<p><strong>Description</strong></p>
<p>This use case outlines the process by which an Admin selects the <strong=
>Custom Landing Page</strong> option, inputs the name of the landing page, =
optionally imports an existing URL, and adds custom content through an HTML=
 editor. After configuring the landing page, the Admin can save the landing=
 page to be used in phishing simulations. This allows for a tailored phishi=
ng campaign where the landing page can mimic real websites or contain custo=
m messages as required.</p>
<p><strong>Actors</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Admin</strong>: Configures the custom landing page, imports a UR=
L if required, and adds custom HTML content.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>System</strong>: Displays the custom landing page configuration =
interface, validates inputs, and saves the landing page.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Preconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Admin is logged into the platform and has access to the <strong>Create N=
ew Campaign</strong> wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Admin is at the <strong>Landing Page</strong> step in the campaign creat=
ion wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Admin has the option to select between <strong>Landing Page</strong>, <s=
trong>Error/404: Page Not Found</strong>, or <strong>Custom Landing Page</s=
trong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Admin has the option to import a landing page from an external URL or ad=
d custom HTML content.</p></li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Postconditions</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>A new <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong> is created and stored in the =
system.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The landing page is available for use in phishing campaigns.</p></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Main Flow (Normal Success Scenario)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Step 1: Navigate to Landing Page Configuration</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin navigates to the <strong>Landing Page</strong> configuration s=
tep in the campaign creation wizard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system displays the <strong>Landing Page Type</strong> options, incl=
uding <strong>Landing Page</strong>, <strong>Error/404: Page Not Found</str=
ong>, and <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin selects the <strong>Custom Landing Page </strong>option.</p></=
li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 2: Enter Landing Page Name</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin enters a <strong>Landing Page Name</strong>: A input field to =
enter a unique Landing Page name. placeholder: Enter unique Landing Page na=
me (max 50 characters)</p></li>
<li>
<p>The <strong>Name</strong> field is a required field for this step.</p></=
li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 3: Import Site (Optional)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin can choose to <strong>Import Site</strong> by clicking on the =
<strong>Import Site</strong> button to clone a web page.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>If the Admin wants to import an existing website to use as the base for =
the custom landing page, they can enter the website URL (e.g., "<a class=3D=
"external-link" href=3D"http://example.com/" rel=3D"nofollow">http://exampl=
e.com</a>").</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system fetches the content from the provided URL and allows the Admi=
n to modify it for the phishing campaign.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 4: Add Custom HTML Content</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin can add custom content in the <strong>HTML</strong> editor sec=
tion.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The editor allows the Admin to write or paste custom HTML code for the l=
anding page.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can use the available text formatting options in the HTML edit=
or (e.g., bold, italics, text alignment, font size).</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can <strong>preview </strong>the content as they edit it and m=
ake changes as needed.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 5: Capture Submitted Data (Optional)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>The Admin can choose to enable the option <strong>Capture Submitted Data=
</strong> if they want to record the data submitted by users on the landing=
 page (e.g., login credentials, personal information). This will utilize We=
bhook feature to capture the data.</p></li>
<li>
<p>This option ensures that any data entered by the target during the phish=
ing simulation is captured and available for analysis.</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 6: Save Custom Landing Page</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>After entering the name and custom content, the Admin clicks <strong>Sav=
e Page</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system validates the input:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Ensures the <strong>Name</strong> field is filled.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Ensures the custom HTML content is not empty (if applicable).</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system saves the custom landing page and confirms the action.</p></l=
i>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Step 7: Confirmation and Exit</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>After successfully saving the custom landing page, the system confirms t=
he action by displaying: "Landing Page saved successfully."</p></li>
<li>
<p>The Admin can click <strong>Exit</strong> to return to the <strong>Campa=
ign Setup</strong> or proceed to the next steps in the campaign creation pr=
ocess.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Frontend Form Validation</strong></p>
<p><strong>Field Validation Rules</strong></p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Name Field</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: This field is mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: The Admin must enter a name for the custom =
landing page.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Landing page name is required."</p></li=
>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>HTML Content</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Required</strong>: The landing page body must not be empty.</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: If the Admin uses the <strong>HTML editor</=
strong>, the content must be valid HTML and not empty.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Landing page content cannot be empty. P=
lease add custom HTML content."</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Import Site URL</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Optional</strong>: Admin can choose to import a site, but this i=
s not mandatory.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: If provided, the URL must be a valid URL fo=
rmat (e.g., <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"http://example.com/" rel=3D"=
nofollow">http://example.com</a>).</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please enter a valid website URL."</p><=
/li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Capture Submitted Data</strong>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Optional</strong>: Admin can enable or disable this option.</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p><strong>Validation</strong>: If enabled, the system will capture and sto=
re the data submitted on the landing page.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Error Message</strong>: "Please enable data capture if required.=
"</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Business Rules</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"a4=
9e163b-55f5-4c53-be40-c7750211b0c1" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Rule</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-1</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must provide a <strong>Name</strong> for the custom landing page b=
efore saving it.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-2</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can <strong>Import Site</strong> by providing a valid URL, or they=
 can manually input <strong>HTML</strong> content.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-3</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can enable <strong>Capture Submitted Data</strong> to record user =
input on the custom landing page.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-4</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system must validate that the <strong>HTML Content</strong> is not e=
mpty if custom content is provided.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-5</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must click <strong>Save Page</strong> after configuring the custom=
 landing page to confirm and store it.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>BR-6</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can preview the custom landing page before saving.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"05=
7167b4-30cb-4a13-aff9-3dfcbd3d7de4" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>ID</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Acceptance Criteria</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Pass/Fail Condition</strong></p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-01</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can enter a <strong>Name</strong> for the custom landing page.</p>=
</td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Name</strong> field is filled and saved successfully.</p></t=
d>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-02</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can <strong>Import Site</strong> by entering a valid website URL.<=
/p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The site is imported and displayed for editing.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-03</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can add custom content using the <strong>HTML editor</strong>.</p>=
</td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Custom HTML content is added and displayed in the editor.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-04</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can enable or disable the <strong>Capture Submitted Data</strong> =
option.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The option is correctly enabled or disabled.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-05</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can <strong>Save Page</strong> after configuring the custom landin=
g page.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The landing page is saved and available for use in campaigns.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-06</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can <strong>Preview</strong> the custom landing page before saving=
 it.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The preview displays the custom landing page content correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-07</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can <strong>Exit</strong> the landing page creation interface afte=
r saving or canceling.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The Admin can exit and return to the campaign setup.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-08</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin must provide a valid <strong>Name</strong> before saving the landi=
ng page.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Save</strong> button is disabled if the <strong>Name</strong=
> field is empty.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-09</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can <strong>Import Site</strong> and view the site content for edi=
ting.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The imported site is editable in the HTML editor.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-10</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>HTML editor</strong> must allow formatting text and insertin=
g HTML elements.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can format the text and add HTML elements correctly.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-11</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can select the <strong>Landing Page Type</strong> as <strong>Custo=
m Landing Page</strong> from the available options.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong> option is selected successfully=
.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-12</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can review the landing page <strong>Preview</strong> before select=
ing the template.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The preview matches the expected custom content.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-13</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can save the custom landing page with the <strong>Save Page</stron=
g> button.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The landing page is saved without errors.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-14</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can use <strong>HTML editor</strong> to modify and view changes in=
stantly.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Changes are displayed instantly in the preview.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-15</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can choose between <strong>importing a site</strong> or <strong>ed=
iting content</strong> manually.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can switch between importing a site or editing content.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-16</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin is warned if the <strong>Name</strong> field is left empty when at=
tempting to save the landing page.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>An error message appears if the <strong>Name</strong> field is empty.</p=
></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-17</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can cancel the process and return to the previous screen.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can click <strong>Cancel</strong> to exit without saving the page.=
</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-18</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can configure and preview a fully functional <strong>Custom Landin=
g Page</strong> using the <strong>HTML editor</strong>.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can preview the final design before saving.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-19</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can adjust the <strong>Capture Submitted Data</strong> functionali=
ty to collect user information if necessary.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can toggle the option on/off to capture data.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>AC-20</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>Admin can configure the <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong> to simulate=
 a realistic phishing attempt.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The <strong>Custom Landing Page</strong> simulates a phishing scenario a=
ccurately.</p></td>
